---
import Logo from '../../../components/Logo.astro'
import StoryCompare from '../../../components/StoryCompare.astro'
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import { pages } from '../../../site'
import { base, kept, mics, notes, renders, shots } from '../../../stories/the-producer'
import '../../../styles/home.css'
import '../../../styles/producer-sleeve.css'

/* The producer: how it was made. The session behind the story (/stories/the-producer), kept off it
   so the story stays the story: what I typed, the takes, the instruments, the track. Static on
   purpose: the story moves, this page is the contact sheet you look at afterwards. */
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How the record was made. The producer, WCGW"
  description="The session behind “The model is the talent. You are the producer.”: what I typed, every take the model made, what I kept, and how the track was built."
  social="The session behind the record: what I typed, every take, what I kept."
  page={pages.theProducerMakingOf}
  image={`${base}/og.png`}
  creator="@raduceuca"
  themeColorLight="#2C4BD4"
  themeColorDark="#2C4BD4"
>
  <div class="sleeve">
    <div class="page">
      <header class="masthead">
        <a class="home" href="/" aria-label="WCGW home"><Logo /></a>
      </header>

      <main>
        <section class="row top" aria-labelledby="title">
          <p class="gutter"><a class="link" href={base}>The record</a></p>
          <div class="body">
            <p class="kicker">WCGW · Liner notes · Making of</p>
            <h1 id="title">How the record was made.</h1>
            <p class="soft">The story is the record. This is the session: what I typed, what came back, what I kept.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="act row" aria-labelledby="pictures">
          <p class="gutter">The pictures</p>
          <div class="body">
            <h2 id="pictures">Same model on every take.</h2>
            <p>Made on 23 November 2026 with <a class="link" href="https://getamplifiers.com" rel="noopener">Amplifiers</a>. What I typed, in order:</p>
            <ol class="notes">
              {notes.map((n) => <li><span class="num">{n.at}</span><q>{n.said}</q></li>)}
            </ol>
          </div>
        </section>

        <figure class="contact">
          <div class="sheet">
            {mics.map((m) => (
              <div>
                <img src={`${base}/mic-take-${m.n}.webp`} alt={m.alt} width="800" height="1000" loading="lazy" />
                <p class="v"><span class="num">Take {m.n}</span> {m.how} {m.verdict}</p>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>
          <figcaption>The microphone, take by take. Same model every time.</figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section class="duo">
          <figure class="cmpfig">
            <StoryCompare
              before={`${base}/again-angled.webp`}
              after={`${base}/again-straight.webp`}
              beforeLabel="Before"
              afterLabel="After"
              alt="The blue AGAIN button seen straight from above, compared with an earlier render seen at an angle on a black module."
            />
            <figcaption>“I want the camera to look straight at the button.” Drag the line.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <div class="body">
            <p class="big">I just kept saying again.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <figure class="takes">
          <ol>
            {shots.map(([file, what], i) => (
              <li class:list={[{ kept: kept.has(file) }]}>
                <img src={`${base}/takes/${file}.webp`} alt={what} width="360" height="360" loading="lazy" />
                <span class="num">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              </li>
            ))}
          </ol>
          <figcaption>
            <abbr class="fact" title={`${renders.made} pictures rendered, ${renders.kept} kept. Amplifiers image sessions, 23 November 2026. Before that, ${renders.drawnRounds} rounds drawn in code.`}>{renders.made} pictures, {renders.kept} kept</abbr>,
            in the order they were made. The rest were demos.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <section class="act row" aria-labelledby="instruments">
          <p class="gutter">The instruments</p>
          <div class="body">
            <h2 id="instruments">More takes, for the instruments.</h2>
            <p>
              That evening the page learned to play, so it needed things to play on. Ten more renders, eight
              kept: the pad controller, then the same controller again with dark translucent pads, the monitor,
              a blank cassette and six labelled ones, each the blank one with a lab’s name pencilled on and its
              own blue. Every part that moves on the page is cut from its own render by a script: the knob caps,
              the woofer cones, the cassette’s hubs, the AGAIN cap going down. The pads’ light is worked out
              from the picture too, one pad at a time. Nothing is drawn twice.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <div class="pair">
          <figure>
            <img src={`${base}/fig-6-pads.webp`} alt="A pocket pad controller in blue plastic: sixteen square pads, four knobs and a small black screen." width="2400" height="1350" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>The pad controller. Fig. 6 in the story.</figcaption>
          </figure>
          <figure class="mon">
            <img src={`${base}/monitor.webp`} alt="A studio monitor in blue plastic, a black woofer and tweeter." width="760" height="819" loading="lazy" />
            <figcaption>The monitor. Two of them stand in the margins once the studio opens.</figcaption>
          </figure>
        </div>

        <section class="act row" aria-labelledby="track">
          <p class="gutter">The track</p>
          <div class="body">
            <h2 id="track">The track.</h2>
            <p>
              Disco in A minor, <span class="fact" title="The tempo the loop is written at: BPM in src/scripts/producer-music.ts. The a cappellas were generated at 122 and stretched to it, pitch kept.">116 BPM</span>.
              Thirty-two channels in eight stems, played in your browser while you read. The band is freely
              licensed samples, one file of 49 hits and notes: a dry kit with a hand-muted snare, a flatwound
              bass, a hollowbody guitar, a 1977 Rhodes, a violin section and a horn section (sources in the
              liner notes). The Moog, the clav, the organ and the lead are synthesised; no free clavinet samples
              exist. The pad is a sampled grand piano in a long room (Salamander Grand Piano by Alexander Holm,
              CC BY 3.0).
            </p>
            <p>
              The singers are ElevenLabs Music, six of them, one per cassette, all singing the same most-AI
              sentences ever written. None is a lab’s own voice. Each a cappella is pitched into A minor, cut
              into its eight lines by a script, and every line is transcribed again to check the cut. Swipe the
              cassettes in Fig. 1 and another singer takes the record.
            </p>
            <p>
              It builds as you read. The piano alone at the top, the singer at A2, the drums at A3, the bass at
              A4, the room at B1. At B2 the desk hands you every fader, and from there on the song is your mix.
            </p>
            <p>
              The records are turntables. The mix plays off a few seconds of tape, so your hand moves the music,
              backwards too. Press your record at the end and the whole song is rendered in your browser, at
              your faders.
            </p>
            <p>Claude wrote the words from my rant and my notes, and built all of it. Every “again” is mine.</p>
            <p><a class="link" href={base}>Back to the record</a>.</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="row liner" aria-labelledby="liner">
          <p class="gutter">Liner notes</p>
          <div class="body">
            <h2 id="liner" class="sr-only">Liner notes</h2>
            <dl class="signs">
              <dt>Notes</dt>
              <dd>Mine, as typed, between 10:50 and 11:50 Bucharest time. Spelling fixed.</dd>
              <dt>Pictures</dt>
              <dd>
                <a class="link" href="https://getamplifiers.com" rel="noopener">Amplifiers</a>.
                <span class="num">{renders.made}</span> rendered, <span class="num">{renders.kept}</span> kept, per its session
                log on 23 November 2026, then ten more for the instruments and the demos, eight kept.
              </dd>
            </dl>
          </div>
        </section>
      </main>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<script>
  // the before/after line follows the range (StoryCompare leaves its behaviour to the page)
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-cmp]').forEach((cmp) => {
    const range = cmp.querySelector('input')
    if (!range) return
    const set = () => cmp.style.setProperty('--x', `${range.value}%`)
    range.addEventListener('input', set)
    set()
  })
</script>

<style>
  .top { padding-top: clamp(2rem, 1rem + 4vw, 4.5rem); }
  .top .gutter .link { color: var(--soft); }
  .kicker { color: var(--soft); font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 0.72em; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  h1 { margin-top: 0.5em; font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 1.2rem + 4.6vw, 4.6rem); line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.022em; text-wrap: balance; }
  h1 + p { margin-top: 1.2rem; }
  .body > p + p { margin-top: var(--beat, 1em); }

  /* what I typed */
  .notes { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin-top: 1.2em; border-top: 1px solid var(--hair); }
  .notes li { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 3.6em minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 0.6em; padding: 0.7em 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hair); line-height: 1.4; }
  .notes .num { color: var(--soft); font-size: 0.78em; padding-top: 0.25em; }
  .notes q { quotes: '“' '”'; }

  /* the microphone, take by take */
  .contact, .duo, .takes, .pair { width: var(--wide); margin: var(--act-space) 0 0; margin-inline: var(--out); }
  .sheet { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; }
  @media (min-width: 44rem) { .sheet { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  .sheet img, .takes img, .pair img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; }
  .v { margin-top: 0.55em; color: var(--soft); font-size: 0.82em; line-height: 1.4; }
  .v .num { display: block; color: var(--ink); font-size: 0.85em; }

  /* before and after */
  .duo { display: grid; gap: 2rem; align-items: center; }
  .duo > .cmpfig { max-width: 24rem; }
  @media (min-width: 52rem) {
    .duo { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 22rem) minmax(0, 1fr); column-gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem); }
    .duo > .cmpfig { max-width: none; }
  }
  .cmpfig :global(.cmp) { background: transparent; border: 0; overflow: visible; }
  .cmpfig :global(.lbl) { background: var(--ink); color: var(--bg); font-family: var(--sans); letter-spacing: 0.06em; }
  .cmpfig :global(.line) { background: var(--ink); }

  /* eighteen takes: the demos struck in pencil */
  .takes ol { list-style: none; padding: 0; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 0.4rem 0.8rem; }
  @media (min-width: 40rem) { .takes ol { grid-template-columns: repeat(6, minmax(0, 1fr)); } }
  .takes li { position: relative; }
  .takes li .num { position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0; font-size: 0.66em; color: var(--soft); }
  .takes li:not(.kept) img { opacity: 0.38; }
  .takes li:not(.kept)::after {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 6%;
    right: 6%;
    top: 46%;
    height: 9%;
    background: var(--pencil);
    -webkit-mask: var(--mark-strike) 0 0 / 100% 100% no-repeat;
    mask: var(--mark-strike) 0 0 / 100% 100% no-repeat;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .takes li:nth-child(3n):not(.kept)::after { -webkit-mask-image: var(--mark-strike-2); mask-image: var(--mark-strike-2); }

  /* the two instrument renders */
  .pair { display: grid; gap: 2rem; align-items: end; }
  @media (min-width: 44rem) { .pair { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 2.2fr) minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .pair .mon img { max-width: 16rem; margin-inline: auto; }

  .liner { margin-top: var(--act-space); padding-top: var(--act-space); border-top: 1px solid var(--hair); }
  .liner .signs { row-gap: 0.45em; font-size: 0.92em; line-height: 1.5; }
  .liner .signs dt { color: var(--soft); }
</style>
